config BR2_PACKAGE_FLIPPER_USB_GADGET
	bool "flipper-usb-gadget"
	depends on BR2_INIT_SYSTEMD # systemd units, .link, udev rules
	help
	  USB-gadget support for Flipper One, shared with the main OS:
	  the configfs gadget engine (usb-gadget-setup.sh) and its preset
	  launchers in /usr/local/bin, the NCM+MSC+MTP composite unit and
	  the Type-C replug helper, the 10-flipusb.link rename and the two
	  udev rules that re-manage flipusb0 in NetworkManager and trigger
	  a replug.

	  Only the composite unit is installed; the other presets' units
	  would let preset-all enable them and race for the single UDC.
	  The composite is started by the enable symlink in the board
	  overlay, and umtprd (BR2_PACKAGE_UMTPRD) serves its MTP function.

	  https://github.com/flipperdevices/flipperone-linux-build-scripts

comment "flipper-usb-gadget needs systemd"
	depends on !BR2_INIT_SYSTEMD
